<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Petrobras receives Iraqi trade mission.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Petrobras receives Iraqi trade mission.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of Brazilian oil monopoly Petrobras is meeting with the members of an Iraqi trade mission, a local news agency said.</p>
<p>Petrobras President Joel Mendes Renno said the company was not negotiating any future oil imports once a United Nations embargo on Iraqi oil had been lifted, according to Invest News.</p>
<p>He said Iraqi trade missions always paid special attention to Petrobras given the company's long partnership with Iraq's State Oil Market Organization (Somo), Invest News said.</p>
</text>
